LATENT DISPATCH
Tue Sep 15 · 4 items · ~3 min

TANAGER-CODER 70B: EARLY ACCESS NOTES
We got a preview. It is very good at multi-file edits and noticeably better than the 34B at reading a codebase before changing it. It is also 2x the price and 3x the latency. For a coding agent that runs overnight, worth it; for autocomplete, no. Public release "early October." https://latentdispatch.ai/p/tanager-70b-preview

SPEND CAPS ARE NOW STANDARD
Every provider we track now offers a per-key or per-project spend ceiling. Six months ago only two did. If you have not set one, the August backfill story from a few weeks back is your cautionary tale.

AN ON-CALL STORY WITH A HAPPY ENDING
An engineer wrote up a 3am page: a customer's data import tripled token volume in an hour, the spend cap tripped, the pipeline paused cleanly, and the on-call went back to sleep. The next morning they raised the cap deliberately. That is what the cap is for. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/oncall-story

SHORT TAKES
· Nimbus adds per-request cost to response headers, matching Quillon.
· Halcyon Vision 3 adds table extraction to structured output.
· Vireo-3 embeddings: 8k context, same price as Vireo-2.

